# JSON Script Interpreter Example

Executes stack-based scripts written in JSON and displays the result using the `NumberDisplayNode`.

## Nodes Used

- `script/jsonInterpreter` — executes JSON script commands on a stack machine
- `output/display/number` — shows the computed result inline

### Supported Script Commands

| Command | Args | Description |
|---------|------|-------------|
| `push` | `[number]` | Push value onto stack |
| `add` | `[]` | Pop two values, push sum |
| `sub` | `[]` | Pop two values, push difference |
| `mul` | `[]` | Pop two values, push product |
| `div` | `[]` | Pop two values, push quotient |
| `dup` | `[]` | Duplicate top of stack |
| `swap` | `[]` | Swap top two values |
| `drop` | `[]` | Discard top of stack |
| `print` | `[]` | No-op (result visible in display) |

### Example Script (computes (5 + 3) * 2 = 16)

```json
[{"cmd":"push","args":[5]},{"cmd":"push","args":[3]},{"cmd":"add","args":[]},{"cmd":"push","args":[2]},{"cmd":"mul","args":[]}]
```

## Graph

1. Add a `JSONScriptInterpreter` node (Scripting → JSON)
2. Set its `script` input to a valid JSON command array
3. Add a `NumberDisplay` node (Output → Value)
4. Connect `JSONScriptInterpreter.result` → `NumberDisplay.value`

## Pre-made Graph

Import `script-demo.json` to load a working graph that computes `(5 + 3) * 2 = 16`.

## Build & Run

```bash
cmake --build --preset debug
./build/debug/examples/script-demo/ScriptDemoApp
```
